## Context

0151 exit criterion: "`erg version` names the algorithm (SHA-256) and exposes
the full digest; the displayed hash is recomputable with stock tools." Today
`version.go:109` prints only the first 12 hex characters (`h[:12]`), does not
name the algorithm, and offers no verification hint. This is a small, clean
code change that unblocks the reproducibility and opsec-documentation work.

## Relevant files
- `src/go/version.go` — `cmdVersion`, line 109 (`h[:12]`)
- `src/go/helptext.go` — help text for version command
- `tests/test_version.sh` — existing version discovery tests
- `tests/test_update.sh` — version output assertions (grep for hash pattern)

## Actions
1. In `cmdVersion` (`version.go`), change `h[:12]` to print the full 64-char
   hex digest, and prefix the line with the algorithm name:
   `  sha256:  <full 64-char hex>`
2. Add a verification hint line to stdout:
   `  verify:  sha256sum tickets/erg`
   (only when the binary path contains `tickets/erg` — the common in-repo case).
3. Update `helpVersion` to document the full digest and the verify hint.
4. Update `test_version.sh` to assert the full 64-char hex and `sha256` label.
5. Update `test_update.sh` hash-pattern assertions (currently match `[0-9a-f]{12}`).
6. Ensure `erg version` for discovered "other binaries" also shows full hash.

## Test
```sh
# Red: assert full SHA-256 in version output
OUT=$(build/erg version)
echo "$OUT" | grep -qE '^\s+sha256:\s+[0-9a-f]{64}$'
```

## Exit criteria
- [ ] `erg version` prints the full 64-char SHA-256 digest
- [ ] The algorithm is named (`sha256:`) in the output
- [ ] A `verify:` hint line shows how to recompute with stock tools
- [ ] Discovered "other binaries" also show full hash
- [ ] `make test` passes (all test suites)
